course: dictionary
lesson: 10342
title: Transferable words and ideas
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Transferable means able to be moved or handed from one person, place or thing to another. Think of a ticket you can give to a friend, or a skill you can use in lots of different places.
explain: Read the words around the word. «Ireland uses the single transferable vote: voters rank candidates, each area elects several people, and votes are counted round by round, which can take days.» The voting words tell you that votes move on from one candidate to another, so transferable fits.
explain: Look for small clues inside the word too. The prefix «non-» means not, so «non-transferable» on a ticket means it cannot be passed to someone else. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «transferable» means can be passed on, does the sentence still make sense? If yes, you have it.
fact: Transferable means able to be moved or handed from one person, place or thing to another.
fact: A transferable ticket or pass can be used by someone else, not only by the buyer.
fact: «Transferable skills» are abilities you can use in many jobs or subjects, like teamwork, problem-solving and clear writing.
fact: The prefix «non-» means not, so «non-transferable» means only the named person may use it.
fact: In science, energy is transferred from one thing to another, so things that can be passed on are transferable.
exercise: A transferable ticket can be used by someone else. What does transferable mean? | *Able to be passed from one person to another | Made of wood | Only for the buyer | Very expensive
exercise: «Ireland uses the single transferable vote: voters rank candidates, each area elects several people, and votes are counted round by round, which can take days.» Which word tells you the counting takes a long time? | candidates | voters | *days | rank
exercise: Teamwork, problem-solving and clear writing are examples of what? | *Transferable skills | Ancient castles | Non-transferable tickets | Forms of energy
test: A «non-transferable» ticket can be used by whom? | Anyone at all | Only the seller | Nobody, ever | *Only the named person
test: Which phrase means skills you can use in many different jobs? | Famished feelings | Barely whispers | Curt replies | *Transferable skills
exam: Which sentence uses transferable correctly? | *Her pass was transferable, so her friend could use it too. | Her pass was transferable, so she felt very tall. | The transferable sky was bright blue. | The transferable castle stood on the hill.
